    "narrative": "The Zurich Zebras enter today\u2019s slate with a heavy emphasis on speed and matchup exploitation, led by **Pete Crow-Armstrong**, who secures our highest efficiency score of 77.20. His matchup against Bradley offers an ideal environment for his elite stolen base profile, bolstered by a 14% platoon advantage and a slow opposing delivery that screams for green lights on the basepaths. Similarly, **Trea Turner** (70.38) is locked into the leadoff spot against Manaea, with wind-aided projections and a favorable dynamic platoon edge making him an essential anchor for our 5x5 Roto production today. **Yordan Alvarez** (68.98) and **Kyle Schwarber** (68.20) also remain high-floor staples; while **Yordan Alvarez** faces a slight negative park adjustment, his elite 0.475 xwOBA effectively renders the venue irrelevant, while **Kyle Schwarber** leverages the same wind-favorable conditions as **Trea Turner** to provide necessary pop in the two-hole.\n\nOur most difficult roster decision involved **Casey Schmitt**, who fell just short of the cut at 48.22. While his 11% platoon advantage against Woo made him a compelling candidate, his lower base projection relative to the starters in the middle infield\u2014specifically **Caleb Durbin**\u2014forced him to the bench to preserve our game caps. **Caleb Durbin** remains a priority start today (52.73) despite a tougher SP matchup, as the combination of a slow opposing delivery and wind-out conditions enhances his stolen base utility in a category where we cannot afford to concede ground. We are also closely monitoring the lineup security of **Dillon Dingler** (52.66); his elevated SP-skill adjustment is tempered by a negative platoon dynamic, yet he remains our most viable option behind the dish. As we navigate the schedule, we are carefully watching **Carson Benge** (39.94) for future usage, but today he remains below our 40.0 efficiency floor, joining **Hyeseong Kim**, **Gary Sanchez**, **Nelson Velazquez**, **Josh Smith**, **Jacob Gonzalez**, **Luis Pena**, and **Pedro Ramirez** in our reserved depth as we look to maximize daily roster efficiency.",
